<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Where a perpendicular bisector meets a circle</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A phone-charging kiosk is to be the same distance from school \(A({@A[1]@}, {@A[2]@})\) as from school \(B({@B[1]@}, {@B[2]@})\), and exactly \({@r@}\) km from the market \(C({@C[1]@}, {@C[2]@})\). Grid units are kilometres.</p><p>(a) The locus of points equidistant from \(A\) and \(B\) is a line.</p><div>\({@lv@} = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) The kiosk can be at two places on this line. Give their \({@av@}\)-coordinates.</p><div>[[input:ans2]] and [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(A\) and \(B\) have the same \({@av@}\)-coordinate, so \(AB\) is [[if test="is(o=0)"]]horizontal[[else]]vertical[[/if]]. Its perpendicular bisector passes through the midpoint \(({@(A[1]+B[1])/2@}, {@(A[2]+B[2])/2@})\) at right angles to \(AB\): \({@lv@} = {@m@}\).</p><p>(b) \(C\) is \({@ca@}\) km from the line \({@lv@} = {@m@}\). A point on the line \({@r@}\) km from \(C\) is \(\sqrt{ {@r@}^2 - {@ca@}^2 } = {@cb@}\) km along the line from the point nearest \(C\), on either side: \({@av@} = {@cc@} - {@cb@} = {@ys[1]@}\) and \({@av@} = {@cc@} + {@cb@} = {@ys[2]@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: where a perpendicular bisector meets a circle. Entries [A, B, C, r, orient, m, [two coordinates]]; the chapter's activity and exercise on this are not repeated. orient 0: AB horizontal, bisector x = m, answers are y-coordinates; orient 1: AB vertical, bisector y = m, answers are x-coordinates. Source: original. */
q61: [[[-1,-1],[9,-1],[10,-2],10,0,4,[-10,6]],[[-4,1],[-4,7],[-3,12],10,1,4,[-9,3]],[[1,-2],[7,-2],[-2,-3],10,0,4,[-11,5]],[[4,-3],[4,5],[2,-3],5,1,1,[-1,5]],[[1,4],[5,4],[12,5],15,0,3,[-7,17]],[[-4,-6],[-4,4],[2,2],5,1,-1,[-2,6]],[[-4,2],[4,2],[-6,3],10,0,0,[-5,11]],[[2,-8],[2,2],[4,9],13,1,-3,[-1,9]],[[-6,-4],[0,-4],[-7,3],5,0,-3,[0,6]],[[1,-1],[1,5],[1,7],13,1,2,[-11,13]]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
A: q61[ix][1]; B: q61[ix][2]; C: q61[ix][3]; r: q61[ix][4]; o: q61[ix][5]; m: q61[ix][6]; ys: sort(q61[ix][7]);
lv: ["x","y"][o+1];
av: ["y","x"][o+1];
/* s: the shared coordinate of A and B (the line AB itself); cp: C's coordinate across the bisector; cc: C's coordinate along it */
s: A[2-o];
cp: C[1+o];
cc: C[2-o];
ca: abs(cp-m);
cb: sqrt(r^2-ca^2);
dl: [cc-r, cc+r];
ta2: ys[1]; ta3: ys[2];]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
