    <node><name>1</name><description>The line AB</description><answertest>NumAbsolute</answertest><sans>ans1</sans><tans>s</tans><testoptions>0.001</testoptions><quiet>0</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>0.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt1-2-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>That is the line through \(A\) and \(B\). The perpendicular bisector crosses \(AB\) at its midpoint, at right angles.</p>]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>-1</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt1-2-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Your line \({@lv@} = {@ans1@}\) meets the line through \(A\) and \(B\) at a point \({@nd(abs(ans1-A[1+o]))@}\) km from \(A\) and \({@nd(abs(ans1-B[1+o]))@}\) km from \(B\). Every point of the locus is the same distance from \(A\) as from \(B\).</p>]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
